WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.774
The v zero comparison begins with exactly the same visible-app brief.

00:00:04.774 --> 00:00:14.322
It asks for three synthetic incidents, an inbox, priority filter, search, selection,
a validated New ticket form and a disconnected AI panel.

00:00:14.322 --> 00:00:22.568
The request keeps the project unpublished, uses only existing included credits, and
prohibits purchases, automatic integrations and real data.

00:00:22.568 --> 00:00:27.776
We do not copy private project credentials or account information from Lovable.

00:00:27.776 --> 00:00:32.550
A new builder project has its own runtime, libraries and permissions.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:36.890
Similar component styling does not make it the same implementation.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:47.740
The first useful comparison is whether a user can complete the same visible journey
and whether the source and capability status explain what actually works.

00:00:48.042 --> 00:00:53.678
A builder may read files, choose dependencies, write components and run its own
checks.

00:00:53.678 --> 00:00:55.691
Those are useful development actions.

00:00:55.691 --> 00:00:59.314
They do not prove that the live preview works.

00:00:59.314 --> 00:01:03.743
Preserve the exact prompt and generation result, then inspect the app.

00:01:03.743 --> 00:01:08.172
If the preview is blank, loading or failed, show that honestly.

00:01:08.172 --> 00:01:15.016
Do not replace it with a mockup of the intended result or a screen from another
builder.

00:01:15.016 --> 00:01:24.275
A repair should be concrete: identify the failed route, dependency or runtime
condition, change the smallest relevant piece, and retest the same journey.

00:01:24.275 --> 00:01:31.120
This recording distinguishes the v zero frontend comparison and porting route from a
fully accepted authenticated agent.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:34.743
The latter requires additional runtime capabilities and separate evidence.

00:01:35.083 --> 00:01:41.033
The model used to generate code and the model called by the finished app remain
separate.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:47.354
Before a new runtime canary, discover the actual available models and select a
suitable lower-cost native option.

00:01:47.354 --> 00:01:52.560
An alias from an old recording is not proof of current availability or cost.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:02:00.369
Do not silently switch to an external gateway, a paid API or a different account
when the intended route is unavailable.

00:02:00.369 --> 00:02:05.203
Keep purchases, subscriptions and credit top-ups outside the build flow unless
explicitly approved.

00:02:05.203 --> 00:02:11.525
If the builder offers a connection to another model account, inspect its data,
permissions and billing boundary.

00:02:11.525 --> 00:02:18.962
The goal of the workshop is to understand these choices, not to make an attractive
answer appear at any cost.

00:02:19.292 --> 00:02:25.104
To reach parity with the accepted Lovable path, the app needs an authenticated
server action.

00:02:25.104 --> 00:02:30.916
The server must know which app user owns the request before making a billable call.

00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:37.116
A quota should use an atomic reservation, so simultaneous requests cannot both pass
a stale check.

00:02:37.116 --> 00:02:40.991
That often needs a supported backend store or transaction mechanism.

00:02:40.991 --> 00:02:46.416
A frontend counter, browser local storage or hidden button is not an equivalent
control.

00:02:46.416 --> 00:02:53.779
In the current v zero comparison, an authenticated and atomic quota backend has not
been established as accepted evidence.

00:02:53.779 --> 00:02:55.716
We keep that gate visible.

00:02:55.716 --> 00:03:05.403
Do not remove authentication, replace it with a hard-coded user, or claim that a
local counter solves the server boundary merely to complete a demo.

00:03:05.708 --> 00:03:29.208
Your turn: follow the manual task. Pause for more time.

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:33.402
The portable part is the capability contract and harness design.

00:03:33.402 --> 00:03:41.369
Preserve the request schema, the early change stop, the small tool registry,
argument validation, execution limits and honest states.

00:03:41.369 --> 00:03:44.723
Adapt the server wrapper to the supported runtime.

00:03:44.723 --> 00:03:48.497
Keep environment values in that runtime's protected server settings.

00:03:48.497 --> 00:03:55.626
The browser should not choose arbitrary model URLs, supply a server key or name a
privileged tool.

00:03:55.626 --> 00:04:04.851
If you export source to work locally, inspect its package manifest and lockfile
first, use the supported toolchain, and preserve a baseline.

00:04:04.851 --> 00:04:14.496
The fact that source can be exported does not mean its managed authentication,
database or model gateway can run unchanged on your laptop.

00:04:14.496 --> 00:04:17.012
Document the adapter work that remains.

00:04:17.333 --> 00:04:24.774
Create or select a distinct Langfuse project for this builder when that destination
and key binding are approved.

00:04:24.774 --> 00:04:28.081
A useful generic name is OpsDesk v zero.

00:04:28.081 --> 00:04:32.214
Use its ingestion key only in this app's server configuration.

00:04:32.214 --> 00:04:40.481
The implementation must produce compatible OpenTelemetry spans and the same safe
export states before the three secret names become meaningful.

00:04:40.481 --> 00:04:45.028
A valid base URL and keypair do not create spans automatically.

00:04:45.028 --> 00:04:49.988
Run at most the specifically approved canary after the backend controls pass.

00:04:49.988 --> 00:04:55.362
Copy its trace and random session privately and independently match the intended
project.

00:04:55.362 --> 00:04:59.909
Until then, label the integration configured, source-backed or unverified as
appropriate.

00:04:59.909 --> 00:05:04.869
Do not call it end-to-end because a settings form accepted the values.

00:05:05.208 --> 00:05:08.138
For each builder, record a small matrix.

00:05:08.138 --> 00:05:11.905
Visible create, search, filter and selection are one row.

00:05:11.905 --> 00:05:13.998
Authenticated native inference is another.

00:05:13.998 --> 00:05:19.439
Bounded tools, atomic quota, early change stop and metadata-only export are separate
rows.

00:05:19.439 --> 00:05:22.787
Independent provider readback is the final telemetry row.

00:05:22.787 --> 00:05:26.136
Give each row its actual status and receipt.

00:05:26.136 --> 00:05:29.065
This makes limitations useful rather than embarrassing.

00:05:29.065 --> 00:05:37.855
A team can decide whether to remain in a managed builder, add a supported backend,
or export and implement an adapter.

00:05:37.855 --> 00:05:43.296
The matrix also prevents the workshop from becoming a contest based on screenshots.

00:05:43.296 --> 00:05:45.807
We care about behavior and evidence.

00:05:45.807 --> 00:05:53.341
The same product can reach that standard through several stacks, but each stack must
earn its acceptance separately.

00:05:53.667 --> 00:05:58.278
Pause if you want to open v zero and inspect your own project.

00:05:58.278 --> 00:06:03.244
Use the visible-app prompt, then test the ordinary controls before asking for an
agent.

00:06:03.244 --> 00:06:06.436
Save the generated source and note the runtime framework.

00:06:06.436 --> 00:06:11.402
List what is frontend only, what is managed, and what needs a server binding.

00:06:11.402 --> 00:06:15.304
You can complete this comparison without making a runtime model call.

00:06:15.304 --> 00:06:21.689
If you have a supported authenticated backend, implement the reviewed harness
controls there and run the bounded tests.

00:06:21.689 --> 00:06:25.946
If you do not, write the missing dependency and continue independent work.

00:06:25.946 --> 00:06:29.847
The lesson is not that a missing feature should be hidden.

00:06:29.847 --> 00:06:36.232
It is that a clear contract lets you choose the next engineering step without losing
the working app.

00:06:36.542 --> 00:07:00.000
Your turn: follow the manual task. Pause for more time.
